x452 text "A0: `fn NAME T... -> T`, lines `ID OP ARG...`, `ret ARG` (or `ret OP ARGS`), `end`. Types u32 bool io, arrays u32x4, records (u32,bool). Params p0 p1... Args: earlier ID, pN, u32 literal, true, false. `use \"file.a0\"` at top links a file. No forward refs or recursion; ops exact mod 2^32.\n"
x453 puts x451 x452
x454 write x453 2
x455 text "mov add sub mul | and or xor (u32 bitwise, or bool logical) | shl shr (count&31) | div (b=0: 4294967295) rem (b=0: a) | eq ne (u32 or bool) lt le gt ge (unsigned) -> bool | select c x y\n"
x456 puts x454 x455
x457 write x456 2
x458 text "call F a... (F earlier) | fold F n s a... state=s; i<n: state=F(state,i,a...) | loop P F n s a... stops when P(...) false\n"
x459 puts x457 x458
x460 write x459 2
x461 text "arr e... | rec e... | text \"s\" | get a i (i mod N) | set a i v | at r k | put r k v (values, no aliasing)\n"
x462 puts x460 x461
x463 write x462 2
x464 text "io: linear token, each value used once. read t->(u32,io) | write t v->io | puts t a->io\n"
x465 puts x463 x464
x466 write x465 2
x467 text "EDIT: first line = shown handle. e0: `id op ...` replaces or inserts before ret; `... @ other` inserts after other; `-id` deletes; `ret x`. g0: `fn ... end` adds/replaces a function; `-fn name` removes.\n"
x468 puts x466 x467
x469 write x468 2
x470 text "Example: fn affine u32 u32 u32 -> u32 / a mul p0 p1 / b add a p2 / ret b / end (one item per line).\n"
