x489 text "A program is a list of functions. A function is a header `fn NAME T... -> T`, then one instruction per line `ID OP ARGS`, then `ret ARG` (or `ret OP ARGS`), then `end`. Parameters are p0, p1, ... Every instruction names a new value; values are immutable. A function may only call functions defined above it, so there is no recursion and the call graph is a DAG. `use \"file.a0\"` at the top of a file links another file into the same namespace."
