x824 text "A view is a function with a handle line on top (e0) and, when the whole program matters, a program handle (g0) with one signature line per function. A reply is the handle line followed by edit lines: `id op ...` replaces an instruction or inserts a new one before ret, `id op ... @ other` inserts after another, `-id` deletes, `ret x` changes the result. Under g0, whole `fn ... end` blocks add or replace functions and `-fn name` removes one. Lines may come in any order that has a valid dependency order, a trailing `end` is fine, and a reply may carry several handle sections applied atomically. Every edit is parsed, typed, and matched against the revision it was written for before it lands; a rejection carries a stable code (parse, type, structure, edit, handle, revision, limit), what was expected, what was found, and the one fix."
