x7516 puts x7514 x7515
x7517 call open x7516 15
x7518 write x7517 2
x7519 text "What happens when an AI makes a mistake?"
x7520 puts x7518 x7519
x7521 call close x7520 
x7522 call open x7521 2
x7523 write x7522 2
x7524 text "The edit is rejected before it lands, with a stable code (parse, type, structure, handle, revision), what was expected, what was found, and the one action that fixes it. The program never changes."
x7525 puts x7523 x7524
x7526 call close x7525 
x7527 call close x7526 
x7528 call open x7527 5
x7529 write x7528 4
x7530 write x7529 2
x7531 text "card reveal"
x7532 puts x7530 x7531
x7533 call open x7532 15
x7534 write x7533 2
x7535 text "Can a wrong program burn compute?"
x7536 puts x7534 x7535
x7537 call close x7536 
x7538 call open x7537 2
x7539 write x7538 2
x7540 text "No. Every function has a static iteration cap, the interpreter has fuel, io output is bounded, and there is no heap, recursion, or unbounded loop. A runaway is impossible by construction."
x7541 puts x7539 x7540
x7542 call close x7541 
x7543 call close x7542 
x7544 call open x7543 5
x7545 write x7544 4
x7546 write x7545 2
x7547 text "card reveal"
x7548 puts x7546 x7547
x7549 call open x7548 15
x7550 write x7549 2
x7551 text "Is the compiler deterministic?"
x7552 puts x7550 x7551
x7553 call close x7552 
x7554 call open x7553 2
x7555 write x7554 2
x7556 text "Yes. No model is involved in compilation. Same source, same bytes, on every target, with content-addressed caching keyed by the semantic revision of each function."
x7557 puts x7555 x7556
x7558 call close x7557 
x7559 call close x7558 
x7560 call open x7559 5
x7561 write x7560 4
x7562 write x7561 2
x7563 text "card reveal"
x7564 puts x7562 x7563
x7565 call open x7564 15
x7566 write x7565 2
x7567 text "How is correctness checked?"
x7568 puts x7566 x7567
x7569 call close x7568 
x7570 call open x7569 2
x7571 write x7570 2
x7572 text "A BigInt oracle runs 5262 generated cases through every backend, the optimizer is proved equivalent to the source with Z3 on all 48 corpus functions, hardware is simulated in Icarus and synthesized in Yosys, and hand-written C, Rust, JavaScript and Python are the benchmark baselines."
x7573 puts x7571 x7572
x7574 call close x7573 
x7575 call close x7574 
x7576 call close x7575 
