x7585 call close x7584 
x7586 call open x7585 5
x7587 write x7586 4
x7588 write x7587 2
x7589 text "limits"
x7590 puts x7588 x7589
x7591 call open x7590 2
x7592 write x7591 2
x7593 text "No floating point, no strings beyond byte arrays, no heap or dynamic sizes (arrays are fixed-length values), no recursion, no exceptions. Whole-task token cost is higher than TypeScript because a new language must ship its primer on every call. The direct native backend covers AArch64 today; x86-64, 32-bit ARM, RISC-V, and AVR are next, and until each passes the corpus it is not listed as supported."
x7594 puts x7592 x7593
x7595 call close x7594 
